<title>GERMANY: Bayer says Q1 profits up five percent.</title>
<headline>Bayer says Q1 profits up five percent.</headline>
<dateline>COLOGNE, Germany 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>German chemicals and drugs group Bayer AG said on Wednesday its first quarter 1997 pre-tax profits rose five percent to 1.218 billion marks ($706.3 million) on turnover of 13.172 billion marks, up from 12.176 billion.</p>
<p>The group said it saw 1997 year profits at least in line with 1996's 2.7 billion marks. In March, the group said it had a realistic chance of topping 1996 profits this year. ($ = 1.724 German Marks)</p>
